# Copy to .env.local (or set in your host) and adjust per environment.

# Base URL of the deployed Mintlify docs site. In dev this defaults to
# http://localhost:3000 (see .env.development). In production this is the live
# Mintlify docs site. If left unset, the code falls back to the same live docs
# URL, so links always resolve.
VITE_DOCS_URL=https://a-identity.mintlify.site

# Base URL of the A-Identity MCP HTTP server.
#  - Local dev: point at your local backend.
#  - Production (Vercel): leave this EMPTY ("") so the frontend calls same-origin
#    paths (/health, /api/*, /mcp). vercel.json then proxies those to the Render
#    backend as first-party requests — this dodges ad blockers / privacy lists that
#    block *.onrender.com and would otherwise show a false "backend offline".
VITE_MCP_URL=http://localhost:3399

# WalletConnect / Reown project id (free, from cloud.reown.com). Enables the
# "WalletConnect (mobile)" option in the wallet picker. Public value (baked into
# the frontend build). Leave unset to hide WalletConnect. Set the same value in
# the Vercel project's env for production.
# VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# ── Analytics (Google Tag Manager / GA4) ──
# Both are optional and BOTH are off unless set: with neither present, no script is
# injected and no request leaves the browser, which keeps local dev and preview
# deploys out of the numbers without anyone remembering to disable something.
# Set these only in the Vercel PRODUCTION environment.
#
# Prefer GTM alone and configure GA4 inside it; setting both loads two tags and
# double-counts every page view. Consent Mode v2 is initialised before either tag
# loads: ad storage and personalisation are denied outright, and analytics storage
# follows the visitor's Do Not Track / Global Privacy Control signal.
# VITE_GTM_ID=GTM-XXXXXXX
# VITE_GA4_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# ── Backend (MCP/REST server) security — set these in the host env (e.g. Render) ──

# Session-token signing secret. REQUIRED in production: without it, tokens are signed
# with a public default and could be forged. On a prod-like host (RENDER / NODE_ENV=
# production / DATABASE_URL set) an unset value falls back to a RANDOM per-process
# secret (safe, but sessions don't survive a restart), and the server logs a warning.
# Set a strong, stable value (>=16 chars) so sessions persist across restarts.
# AUTH_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# CORS allowlist: comma-separated origins allowed to call the API cross-origin.
# Unset → '*' (fine for local Vite dev). In production set it to your site origin(s);
# the prod frontend uses a same-origin Vercel proxy, so this locks out other origins.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://a-identity.xyz,https://a-identity.vercel.app

# Number of trusted reverse proxies in front of the backend (Render/Vercel = 1). The rate
# limiter derives the client IP from the X-Forwarded-For entry this many hops from the end,
# so a spoofed XFF can't hand each request a fresh bucket. Default 1.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT=1

# Session-token lifetime in ms (default 7 days). A leaked bearer token expires after this.
# AUTH_TOKEN_TTL_MS=604800000

# Circle developer platform (console.circle.com). With this set, the MCP server's
# /api/circle and get_circle_status perform a real authenticated ping.
# Sandbox keys look like TEST_API_KEY:<id>:<secret>.
# CIRCLE_API_KEY=
# CIRCLE_API_BASE=https://api.circle.com

# ── Circle on-chain rails (x402, Nanopayments, Gateway, CCTP) ──
# These are PERMISSIONLESS on Arc testnet — they need NO Circle API key. The only
# credential is the signer that broadcasts writes: ARC_SIGNER_KEY (a funded Arc key;
# see README "Going live"). Without it, every rail returns a clean `prepared` no-op.
#   - Nanopayments/x402 seller receiving address (optional; defaults to the signer):
# X402_PAY_TO=0x...
#   - ARC_SIGNER_KEY is read from the process env directly (not this Vite file); set it
#     inline or via the host env panel — see README.

# ── ERC-4337 session-key smart account (idea C2) ──
# The real account-abstraction session key uses a Pimlico bundler on Arc testnet. Get a
# free key at pimlico.io. Credential-gated: without it, /api/arc/session-key-demo returns
# a clean `prepared` no-op. Needs a funded ARC_SIGNER_KEY too (it funds the smart account
# for its own UserOp gas). Backend-only (read from process env, not this Vite file).
# PIMLICO_API_KEY=pim_...

# Passwordless email sign-in ("magic link") via Resend (resend.com). Backend-only,
# credential-gated: without RESEND_API_KEY the email path cleanly reports "not
# configured" and the UI falls back to wallet / guest. Set these in the Render env.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# MAGIC_FROM_EMAIL=A-Identity <onboarding@resend.dev>   # verify a domain to email arbitrary addresses (test sender only reaches your own)
# APP_URL=https://a-identity.vercel.app                 # base URL the emailed link points back to

# ── Per-chain signers and RPCs (backend-only, read from process env) ──
# One pair per chain in mcp/src/chains/registry.ts, named exactly as that chain's
# descriptor declares them (`signerEnvVar` / `rpcEnvVar`). These are the ONLY supported
# way to give a chain a key or a private endpoint: the code derives both from the
# descriptor, so there is nothing to wire beyond setting the variable.
#
# Every signer is optional and every one is fail-clean: without it, that chain's writes
# return a labeled `prepared` no-op instead of broadcasting. Every RPC is optional too and
# falls back to the descriptor's public endpoint. Leave the values EMPTY here - a real key
# belongs in the host env panel (Render), never in a file that ships with the repo.

# Circle Arc testnet (eip155:5042002) - the chain the app is built on
# ARC_SIGNER_KEY=
# ARC_RPC_URL=

# Stellar. Both networks name themselves explicitly, and the bare STELLAR_SIGNER_SECRET
# that used to mean "testnet" is RETIRED rather than repointed. Every other chain here
# uses the bare name for mainnet and a _TESTNET_ variant for the testnet, but following
# that convention would have silently turned an existing testnet value into a pubnet
# signing key the next time someone pulled. A variable that changes which network it
# signs on is worse than a variable that does not exist. "pubnet" and "testnet" are also
# Stellar's own words for these networks, so this is the native spelling, not a special
# case. The secret is a Stellar S... ed25519 seed, not a 0x hex key.

# Stellar pubnet (stellar:pubnet) - real money. See soroban/SECURITY-REVIEW.md before setting.
# STELLAR_PUBNET_SIGNER_SECRET=
# STELLAR_PUBNET_RPC_URL=

# Stellar testnet (stellar:testnet)
# STELLAR_TESTNET_SIGNER_SECRET=
# STELLAR_TESTNET_RPC_URL=

# Algorand (beta pair). The signer is a 25-word Algorand mnemonic, not a hex key. Unset
# means every Algorand write path is a labeled no-op; reads fall back to the public
# Nodely endpoints in the registry. The payTo account must be opted in to the USDC ASA
# before the x402 rail can serve a challenge (0.1 ALGO minimum-balance step).
# ALGORAND_MAINNET_SIGNER_MNEMONIC=
# ALGORAND_MAINNET_RPC_URL=
# ALGORAND_TESTNET_SIGNER_MNEMONIC=
# ALGORAND_TESTNET_RPC_URL=
#
# The Algorand x402 rail (x402 v2 "exact" through the GoPlausible facilitator).
# NETWORKS is a CSV of registry CAIP-2 ids; unset means the rail refuses with 501.
# The payTo account must exist and be opted in to the USDC ASA before anything settles.
# X402_ALGORAND_NETWORKS=
# X402_ALGORAND_PAYTO=
# X402_ALGORAND_MAINNET_PAYTO=
# X402_ALGORAND_TESTNET_PAYTO=
# X402_ALGORAND_FACILITATOR=
# X402_ALGORAND_TAG=
# X402_ALGORAND_MIN_VALUE_USD=
# X402_ALGORAND_MAX_VALUE_USD=
# ALGORAND_MAINNET_INDEXER_URL=
# ALGORAND_TESTNET_INDEXER_URL=

# OKX X Layer mainnet (eip155:196) - identity reads are live; the public RPC caps getLogs
# XLAYER_SIGNER_KEY=
# XLAYER_RPC_URL=

# Base mainnet (eip155:8453)
# BASE_SIGNER_KEY=
# BASE_RPC_URL=

# Avalanche C-Chain (eip155:43114) - planned
# AVAX_SIGNER_KEY=
# AVAX_RPC_URL=

# Arbitrum One (eip155:42161) - planned
# ARB_SIGNER_KEY=
# ARB_RPC_URL=

# Robinhood Chain testnet (eip155:46630)
# RHCHAIN_TESTNET_SIGNER_KEY=
# RHCHAIN_TESTNET_RPC_URL=

# Robinhood Chain mainnet (eip155:4663) - the documented public endpoint is rate limited,
# so production traffic needs a private one here
# RHCHAIN_SIGNER_KEY=
# RHCHAIN_RPC_URL=

# Celo mainnet (eip155:42220)
# CELO_SIGNER_KEY=
# CELO_RPC_URL=

# Celo Sepolia testnet (eip155:11142220)
# CELO_SEPOLIA_SIGNER_KEY=
# CELO_SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=

# ── Stellar x402 rail (mcp/src/x402-stellar/) ──
# The Soroban sibling of the EIP-3009 rail. Same discipline: unconfigured answers 501 and
# never serves for free, and nothing is recorded as settled until we have read the
# transfer event off the ledger ourselves.
#
# Which networks the rail sells on, comma separated, in CAIP-2. The first is the default
# when a request does not name one.
# X402_STELLAR_NETWORKS=stellar:testnet
#
# The G... account that receives payment. It MUST already hold a USDC trustline or every
# settlement fails with op_no_trust, which reads to a buyer as our bug.
# X402_STELLAR_PAYTO=
#
# Who assembles and broadcasts the buyer's signed authorization entry.
#   self = we do it, paying the network fee from the chain's own signer above. This is
#          what we do on every EVM chain, and it is the default when a signer is present.
#   oz   = OpenZeppelin Channels does it. A real third party, and the fallback.
# Either way the buyer signs an authorization entry and needs no XLM.
# X402_STELLAR_FACILITATOR=self
#
# OZ Channels credentials, needed only on the `oz` path. Required on BOTH networks; there
# is no anonymous tier. Generate at channels.openzeppelin.com/testnet/gen (testnet) and
# channels.openzeppelin.com/gen (mainnet) - a plain GET returns {"apiKey": "..."}.
# Two variables, not one plus a switch, for the same reason the signers are split above.
# X402_STELLAR_TESTNET_OZ_KEY=
# X402_STELLAR_PUBNET_OZ_KEY=
#
# Optional: a dedicated fee payer for the `self` path, so the account paying network fees
# can be a thin XLM-only wallet separate from the chain's general signer. Falls back to the
# chain descriptor's signerEnvVar when unset. Network-scoped, like everything else here.
#
# These replace X402_STELLAR_SIGNER_SECRET, which was read by the rail's readiness check
# and by nothing that signs, so setting it made the rail report itself ready while nothing
# could actually broadcast. If you have it set, move the value here.
# X402_STELLAR_TESTNET_FEE_PAYER=
# X402_STELLAR_PUBNET_FEE_PAYER=

# Who may be settled FOR. We assemble the transaction and pay the network fee, so /settle
# is allowlisted by default. G... accounts, compared EXACTLY: a StrKey is case-significant
# base32, and lowercasing one produces a string that matches nothing.
# X402_STELLAR_ALLOWED_PAYTO=
# true accepts any payTo, which makes settle an XLM faucet with our name on it. Off unless
# somebody turns it on deliberately.
# X402_STELLAR_PUBLIC_SETTLE=

# The economic guards, in the units Stellar actually uses: stroops, not wei, and LEDGERS,
# not seconds. Expiry is a ledger number, and dividing by an assumed five-second close time
# would put a guess inside the decision. The defaults are sized against a measurement
# rather than a feeling: one real settlement cost 22,973 stroops, so a 1,000,000 stroop
# ceiling is about 43 times normal, and the daily budget is 100 of those.
# X402_STELLAR_MIN_VALUE_USD=0.0001
# X402_STELLAR_MAX_VALUE_USD=1
# X402_STELLAR_EXPIRY_HEADROOM_LEDGERS=12
# X402_STELLAR_MAX_FEE_STROOPS=1000000
# X402_STELLAR_DAILY_FEE_STROOPS=100000000

# --- Stellar x402 BUYER side (scripts/x402-stellar-buyer.mjs only) ----------------
# Nothing on the server reads these. They belong to the buyer script, which is the other
# half of the rail: it takes a 402, signs a Soroban authorization entry and retries. The
# buyer pays no network fee on this rail, so this account needs USDC and a trustline for
# it, and nothing else. Use a DEDICATED account: a seed here is not a fee payer and must
# never be one, because the fee payer signs envelopes and this one signs authorizations.
# X402_STELLAR_BUYER_SECRET=S...
# Optional. Overrides the simulation RPC; the default comes from the chain registry.
# X402_STELLAR_BUYER_RPC=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
